WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:09.640
Obviously,

2
00:00:09.649 --> 00:00:11.800
the business continuity plan needs to be

3
00:00:11.810 --> 00:00:14.529
maintained somewhere where it can be accessed

4
00:00:14.859 --> 00:00:17.090
often in modern organizations,

5
00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:20.479
everything is digital and not provided as a hard copy.

6
00:00:20.969 --> 00:00:23.159
This can be dangerous just like storing

7
00:00:23.170 --> 00:00:25.280
everything within the main company building.

8
00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:29.350
Some organizations have what is called the red book,

9
00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:33.020
which is given to the appropriate individual outside the facility.

10
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.229
All the procedures are outlined in that document

11
00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:39.169
in case for example, a hurricane hits

12
00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:41.450
the power is out and all the facilities are

13
00:00:41.459 --> 00:00:44.830
compromised and there is no access to electronic backups.

14
00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:47.540
It is important to update this hard copy red

15
00:00:47.549 --> 00:00:50.340
book any time the electronic copy is updated.

16
00:00:50.349 --> 00:00:52.630
So both versions remain consistent.